ly! Using the distributive property can simplify the multiplication of large numbers by breaking them down into smaller, more manageable parts. The distributive property states that \\(a \\times (b + c) = a \\times b + a \\times c\\). We can apply this property to break down the multiplication of 123456789 by 987654321 into smaller multiplications.\n\nLet's break down the numbers:\n\n1. **Express 987654321 as \\(1000000000 - 113445678\\):**\n   \\[\n   987654321 = 1000000000 - 113445678\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   123456789 \\times 987654321 = 123456789 \\times (1000000000 - 113445678)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 123456789 \\times 1000000000 - 123456789 \\times 113445678\n   \\]\n\n3. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   - First part: \\(123456789 \\times 1000000000\\)\n   - Second part: \\(123456789 \\times 113445678\\)\n\n4. **Calculate \\(123456789 \\times 1000000000\\):**\n   \\[\n   123456789 \\times 1000000000 = 123456789000000000\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate \\(123456789 \\times 113445678\\):**\n   \\[\n   123456789 \\times 113445678 = 141932631145580489\n   \\]\n\n6. **Subtract the second part from the first part:**\n   \\[\n   123456789000000000 - 141932631145580489\n   \\]\n\n   To perform this subtraction, align the numbers by their place values and subtract:\n   ```\n   123456789000000000\n   -141932631145580489\n   ---------------\n   81424157854419511\n   ```\n\nTherefore, using the distributive property, the product of 123456789 and 987654321 is \\(81424157854419511\\).\n\nThis method can be more efficient for mental calculations or when dealing with very large numbers. <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Therefore, using the distributive property, the product of 123456789 and 987654321 is \\(81424157854419511\\). <|User|>Thank you for the detailed explanation. This method seems much more efficient for large numbers.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>You're welcome! Using the distributive property can indeed make large number multiplications more 